pokeplatinum-tags.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): Smooth motion's tags, the pseudo-command
that names the game object each 3D list belongs to (libntr's simulator/sim_g3tag.h), so the in-betweens can pair sprites,
shadows, effects and particles by identity. Sites: billboard.c BillboardList_Draw (a field sprite: its list, the billboard,
the texture and palette indexes its animation shows), overworld_anim_manager.c OverworldAnimManagerList_Render (a field
effect: its render function, the anim manager), the two shadow render functions of overlay005/ov5_021F134C.c (inst = the
map object's sprite's, the anchor), lib/spl's two particle draw loops (the emitter, the particle, its age); each loop ends
with the empty tag. The places that make a billboard, an anim manager, an emitter or a particle again drop its old id
(SIM_G3TagDrop). Off (the default) each site is one flag test and the command stream is unchanged; BWPORT_VCAPTURE_TAGS=1
or SIM_G3TagEnable(1) turns them on. The DS build never sees the patch.
